  "arrangerNotes": "Chorus (refrain), vocal line, transcribed by visual reading of the original 1927 Irving Berlin Inc. sheet music (scan and LilyPond transcription saved in scores/b10/), key G major, cut time (durations in quarter-note beats). The middle section is played twice, as printed (two lyric lines each time). Simplification: the two chromatic E flats (the flattened 6th on 'shining' and on 'hurrying') are played as 6 (E natural), the nearest drum note. Range low 5 to 6. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums).",
